          <hcontainer name="part" eId="schedule-1__part-3">
            <num>3</num>
            <heading>Application and saving provisions</heading>
            <hcontainer name="clause" eId="schedule-1__part-3__clause-27">
              <num>27</num>
              <heading>Application provision</heading>
              <content>
                <p>The amendments made by this Schedule apply in relation to a statutory declaration made on or after the commencement of this Schedule.</p>
              </content>
            </hcontainer>
            <hcontainer name="clause" eId="schedule-1__part-3__clause-28">
              <num>28</num>
              <heading>Saving provision—prescribed persons</heading>
              <content>
                <p>A person who was, immediately before the commencement of this Schedule, prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 8(b) of the <i>Statutory Declarations Act 1959</i>, as in force immediately before that commencement, is taken, on and after that commencement, to be prescribed by the regulations to be a prescribed person for the purposes of the definition of <b><i>prescribed person</i></b> in <ref href="#sec-4">section 4</ref> of that Act, as amended by this Schedule.</p>
                <p>[<i>Minister’s second reading speech made in—</i></p>
                <p><i>House of Representatives on 7 September 2023</i></p>
                <p><i>Senate on 14 September 2023</i>]</p>
                <p>(107/23)</p>
              </content>
            </hcontainer>
